[38;2;124;124;124mk≥1. Similarly all three are even. So ab-c, bc-a, ca-b all even.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mIf two are odd and one even, say a,b odd, c even: ab-c = odd-even = odd, so ab-c[0m[38;2;124;124;124m= 1 (only odd power of 2). bc-a = even-odd = odd, so bc-a = 1. ca-b = even-odd =[0m[38;2;124;124;124modd, so ca-b = 1. Then ab-c=1 and bc-a=1: ab-1=c and bc-1=a. From ab-1=c: [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mc=ab-1. From bc-1=a: b(ab-1)-1=a → ab²-b-1=a → a(b²-1)=b+1 → a(b-1)(b+1)=(b+1) →[0m[38;2;124;124;124ma(b-1)=1 → a=1, b=2. But a,b odd, contradiction.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mIf one is odd and two even, say a odd, b,c even: ab-c = even-even = even. bc-a =[0m[38;2;124;124;124meven-odd = odd, so bc-a=1. ca-b = even-even = even. So bc-a=1 → bc=1+a. Since [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mb,c even, bc is divisible by 4, so 1+a ≡ 0 mod 4, a ≡ 3 mod 4. Also ab-c is even[0m[38;2;124;124;124mpower of 2, ca-b is even power of 2.[0m

