[38;2;124;124;124m(ab-c)(ca-b) = a²bc - ab² - c²a + bc = a(bc·a - b² - c²) + bc... this is getting[0m[38;2;124;124;124mmessy.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me try: (ab-c) + (ca-b) = a(b+c) - (b+c) = (a-1)(b+c). Wait:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(ab-c) + (ca-b) = ab + ca - c - b = a(b+c) - (b+c) = (a-1)(b+c).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo (a-1)(b+c) = 2^u + 2^w.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSimilarly:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(b-1)(a+c) = 2^u + 2^v[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(c-1)(a+b) = 2^v + 2^w[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThese are very useful![0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo we have:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- (a-1)(b+c) = 2^u + 2^w[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- (b-1)(a+c) = 2^u + 2^v[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- (c-1)(a+b) = 2^v + 2^w[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe right-hand sides are sums of two powers of 2.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mA sum of two powers of 2: 2^p + 2^q. If p=q, this is 2^(p+1). If p≠q, say p<q, [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mthis is 2^p(1 + 2^(q-p)), which has 2-adic valuation p.[0m

